WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.480
The original Star Wars trilogy remains one
of the most successful and popular film series

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.689
in history.

00:00:06.689 --> 00:00:10.490
So when it came time to cast the prequels
in the late '90s, George Lucas had a tall

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.219
task ahead of him — and his casting choices
didn't always pan out.

00:00:14.219 --> 00:00:18.020
Whether you love or hate the Star Wars prequels,
though, there's no denying the franchise might

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.610
have been very different if some of the big
name stars Lucas had considered were in the

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.610
films instead.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.520
Here's a look at some of the A-list celebrities
who were almost in the Star Wars prequels.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.039
Leonardo DiCaprio as Anakin Skywalker

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:33.440
By the time Attack of the Clones began filming
in 2000, Leonardo DiCaprio had become the

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.769
hottest young heartthrob in Hollywood with
films like Titanic.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:40.840
DiCaprio met with Lucas about playing Anakin
Skywalker in the second and third Star Wars

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.300
prequels, but ultimately turned down the role
because, despite his superstar status, he

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.970
didn't feel ready for the kind of attention
that Star Wars would bring.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.440
It was the second time he almost romanced
Natalie Portman on screen: she was originally

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:57.050
cast opposite DiCaprio in Romeo + Juliet,
but dropped out because she was so young at

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.550
the time that her scenes with DiCaprio were
unintentionally creepy.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.160
Good thing she avoided all that creepy romance,
right?

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.180
Oh, wait.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:09.910
“I’m haunted by the kiss that you should
never have given me.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:15.750
My heart is beating, hoping that that kiss
will not become a scar.”

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.750
Whoops.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.940
Christian Bale as Anakin Skywalker

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:23.250
Years before Christian Bale donned Batman's
iconic cape and cowl, he was almost a very

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.680
different type of dark knight.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.120
In the lead-up to Attack of the Clones, Lucasfilm
casting director Robin Gurland reviewed over

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.310
700 tapes, hoping to find the perfect Anakin
Skywalker.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:37.170
One name that reportedly came up: Christian
Bale, who had worked with George Lucas' close

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.300
friend Steven Spielberg on Empire of the Sun,
and was coming off a critically acclaimed

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.630
performance as a gleefully murderous businessman
in 2000's American Psycho.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.580
The role went to Hayden Christensen instead,
however.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.920
Oh, what might have been.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.620
“What are you talking about?”

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.630
Nothing!

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.280
Everything's cool, man.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.810
Colin Hanks as Anakin Skywalker

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:02.690
Like DiCaprio and Bale, Colin Hanks, son of
Tom Hanks, also lost the role of Anakin Skywalker

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:03.690
to Hayden Christensen.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.690
The reason?

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:08.090
Because Christensen's chemistry with Portman
— who was already cast to play Queen Amidala

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.319
— was apparently too good to miss.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:14.340
Hanks probably dodged a bullet: he has a thriving
career, while Christensen is known as the

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.690
guy who ruined Darth Vader.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.920
"I hate you!"

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.750
The feeling is mutual, buddy.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.260
Tupac Shakur as Mace Windu

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:27.810
The role of Mace Windu seemed to have been
written specifically for lifelong Star Wars

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.850
fan Samuel L. Jackson.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:34.310
But before Jackson got the part, Lucas actually
auditioned other actors for the role — including

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.590
legendary rapper Tupac Shakur!

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:40.340
According to Rick Clifford, an audio engineer
at Death Row Records who often spoke with

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.520
Tupac about the rapper's budding acting career,
Tupac auditioned for Lucas sometime in 1996,

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.890
shortly before The Phantom Menace started
filming.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.650
Unfortunately, Tupac died in a still-unresolved
drive-by shooting later that year, Jackson

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.110
ended up with the part, and the rest is history.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.410
"This party's over."

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.530
Benicio Del Toro as Darth Maul

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:03.410
If there's a single good thing that came out
of The Phantom Menace, it's Darth Maul.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.430
The guy looks cool, uses a supercool double
lightsaber, and actually made brief moments

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:08.990
of the film watchable.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:13.230
Before newcomer Ray Park took over the role,
Benicio Del Toro was cast as the spiky Sith

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.230
Lord.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.180
But Del Toro, who has a face built for villainy,
left the role when George Lucas cut out most

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.860
of Maul's speaking parts, leaving only a lot
of fancy gymnastics.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:26.270
Good news though: Del Toro will be returning
to the Star Wars universe in Episode VIII.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.640
Michael Jackson as Jar Jar Binks

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.099
Of course, for all the good that Darth Maul
brought, there's...this guy.

00:03:32.099 --> 00:03:36.569
Yes, Jar Jar Binks, that infamous weirdo from
another planet, is unquestionably the most

00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:39.220
controversial character in the Star Wars universe.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:43.060
Now imagine how much more controversial he
would have been if he had been played by Michael

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.540
Jackson, that infamous weirdo from another
planet.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.720
Yes, it's true: while The Phantom Menace was
filming in London, Lucas introduced Jar Jar

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.480
actor Ahmed Best to Michael Jackson.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.040
And as it turned out, Jackson had wanted the
role first.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.420
“Michael was kind of lobbying for the role.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:02.600
He really wanted to do it, but he wanted to
do it with like, prosthetics and makeup.”

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.379
Lucas wanted to create a fully computer-generated
character, however, so he cast Best in the

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:07.379
role instead.

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:08.879
At least we'll always have Captain Eo!

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:17.949
Thanks for watching!

00:04:17.949 --> 00:04:20.440
